1
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:07,679
Last time, we asked:

2
00:00:07,699 --> 00:00:09,509
Two ring magnets on a pencil!

3
00:00:09,769 --> 00:00:13,299
The top one floats in mid-air, with no glue and no string.

4
00:00:13,579 --> 00:00:14,799
What holds it up?

5
00:00:14,852 --> 00:00:16,002
One, a pull.

6
00:00:17,242 --> 00:00:18,292
Two, a push.

7
00:00:19,763 --> 00:00:21,273
Hold on to your answer!

8
00:00:23,145 --> 00:00:26,605
Today, we find out where a magnet pulls the hardest, and how

9
00:00:26,625 --> 00:00:27,935
a magnet can push!

10
00:00:28,442 --> 00:00:30,922
A little spider is hiding in this video.

11
00:00:31,172 --> 00:00:32,412
Can you spot it?

12
00:00:32,533 --> 00:00:34,393
Spiders love quiet corners.

13
00:00:34,453 --> 00:00:35,733
Look in the corners!

14
00:00:35,784 --> 00:00:37,244
You against the Buddies!

15
00:00:37,514 --> 00:00:39,364
Lock in first with your fingers.

16
00:00:39,634 --> 00:00:41,464
One finger for every point.

17
00:00:42,045 --> 00:00:43,195
Today you'll learn:

18
00:00:43,397 --> 00:00:44,417
Two poles.

19
00:00:44,614 --> 00:00:46,164
Where the pull is strongest.

20
00:00:46,363 --> 00:00:47,713
Attract and repel.

21
00:00:48,215 --> 00:00:49,155
Are you ready?

22
00:00:49,595 --> 00:00:50,365
Three!

23
00:00:50,745 --> 00:00:51,405
Two!

24
00:00:51,775 --> 00:00:52,425
One!

25
00:00:52,845 --> 00:00:53,565
Go!

26
00:00:54,954 --> 00:00:55,844
Round one!

27
00:00:56,164 --> 00:00:57,744
What holds up the top ring?

28
00:00:58,034 --> 00:00:59,344
Show me your fingers!

29
00:01:02,815 --> 00:01:03,795
Locked in!

30
00:01:03,923 --> 00:01:04,793
One, a pull!

31
00:01:05,163 --> 00:01:07,573
Magnets attract, and attract means pull.

32
00:01:07,653 --> 00:01:09,353
We learnt that last time!

33
00:01:09,401 --> 00:01:10,281
Two.

34
00:01:10,451 --> 00:01:13,341
When I press the top ring down, I can feel it pushing

35
00:01:13,361 --> 00:01:14,811
back up on my finger.

36
00:01:14,859 --> 00:01:15,789
Two, a push!

37
00:01:15,919 --> 00:01:18,139
A pull would bring it down onto the other ring.

38
00:01:18,339 --> 00:01:20,099
Something must be pushing it up!

39
00:01:20,375 --> 00:01:21,945
Be the top ring magnet!

40
00:01:22,225 --> 00:01:23,215
Shrink down.

41
00:01:23,495 --> 00:01:24,425
Quietly.

42
00:01:26,710 --> 00:01:30,380
You are a ring magnet, sliding down a pencil like a pole

43
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:31,480
at the playground.

44
00:01:32,230 --> 00:01:34,590
Below you is another ring magnet.

45
00:01:35,115 --> 00:01:36,945
Closer, and you slow down.

46
00:01:37,725 --> 00:01:40,435
Something you cannot see is pushing up on you.

47
00:01:41,215 --> 00:01:43,785
You stop in mid-air, and bob gently.

48
00:01:44,293 --> 00:01:45,733
Pip presses you down.

49
00:01:46,513 --> 00:01:48,843
The closer you get, the harder the push.

50
00:01:49,623 --> 00:01:51,733
He lets go, and up you spring!

51
00:01:52,246 --> 00:01:53,266
Look down.

52
00:01:54,036 --> 00:01:56,916
Between the rings is a gap with nothing in it.

53
00:01:57,686 --> 00:01:59,416
No glue, and no string.

54
00:02:00,276 --> 00:02:01,386
Just a push.

55
00:02:03,037 --> 00:02:04,947
The answer is two: a push!

56
00:02:05,197 --> 00:02:06,777
Did you show two fingers?

57
00:02:07,017 --> 00:02:08,417
Put one finger up!

58
00:02:08,437 --> 00:02:11,007
The bottom ring pushes up on the top ring.

59
00:02:11,167 --> 00:02:13,357
So the top ring floats on the push!

60
00:02:13,484 --> 00:02:16,214
Which part of a magnet pulls and pushes the most?

61
00:02:16,304 --> 00:02:19,474
I think it is the middle, because it is the biggest part!

62
00:02:20,123 --> 00:02:21,273
Look closer.

63
00:02:21,863 --> 00:02:25,393
Dip a bar magnet into the steel paper clips from our class

64
00:02:25,413 --> 00:02:26,746
stationery tray.

65
00:02:26,766 --> 00:02:27,866
Lift it up.

66
00:02:28,476 --> 00:02:30,926
The clips hang in bunches at the two ends.

67
00:02:31,496 --> 00:02:33,189
The middle has hardly any.

68
00:02:33,209 --> 00:02:35,949
These two ends are the magnet's poles.

69
00:02:37,209 --> 00:02:40,449
Every magnet has two poles: a North pole and a South pole.

70
00:02:40,469 --> 00:02:45,027
On this magnet, North is painted red, and South is painted blue!

71
00:02:45,047 --> 00:02:49,447
The bar magnet has the strongest pull or attraction at the two

72
00:02:49,467 --> 00:02:50,347
poles.

73
00:02:51,473 --> 00:02:53,693
Attraction is another word for the pull.

74
00:02:53,773 --> 00:02:56,649
It is strongest at the two poles, not in the middle!

75
00:02:56,669 --> 00:02:59,739
Every magnet has two poles, whatever its shape.

76
00:03:00,299 --> 00:03:03,839
A ring magnet's poles are on its two flat sides, one on

77
00:03:03,859 --> 00:03:05,909
top, and one underneath.

78
00:03:08,606 --> 00:03:09,906
Say it with me!

79
00:03:10,615 --> 00:03:12,335
A magnet has two poles.

80
00:03:12,805 --> 00:03:14,865
It has a North pole and a South pole.

81
00:03:15,395 --> 00:03:18,745
A magnet has two poles where attraction is the strongest.

82
00:03:21,372 --> 00:03:22,452
My turn!

83
00:03:22,672 --> 00:03:25,782
The top ring will not come down to touch the other ring.

84
00:03:26,032 --> 00:03:28,892
Magnets attract, so this ring must be broken!

85
00:03:29,021 --> 00:03:30,581
Something is not right.

86
00:03:30,851 --> 00:03:33,031
If you can spot it, cross your arms.

87
00:03:33,311 --> 00:03:34,271
Hold on!

88
00:03:39,684 --> 00:03:40,814
Arms crossed?

89
00:03:41,084 --> 00:03:42,294
One finger up!

90
00:03:42,346 --> 00:03:45,326
Watch! I turn the top ring over and let it go.

91
00:03:45,536 --> 00:03:46,186
Click!

92
00:03:46,346 --> 00:03:47,706
It snaps right down.

93
00:03:47,816 --> 00:03:49,346
It is not broken at all!

94
00:03:49,472 --> 00:03:51,972
The floating ring was pushed, not broken.

95
00:03:52,100 --> 00:03:54,570
So the same two magnets can push and pull?

96
00:03:54,650 --> 00:03:56,030
How does that work?

97
00:03:56,681 --> 00:03:57,811
Look closer.

98
00:03:58,391 --> 00:04:02,102
Two bar magnets lie on round pencils, so they can roll.

99
00:04:02,122 --> 00:04:05,932
A red end and a blue end: they roll together and click,

100
00:04:05,952 --> 00:04:07,435
even before they touch.

101
00:04:07,455 --> 00:04:08,965
Now turn one round.

102
00:04:09,535 --> 00:04:12,415
Two red ends: one magnet rolls away.

103
00:04:12,985 --> 00:04:14,542
The gap never closes.

104
00:04:14,562 --> 00:04:18,522
When magnets push each other away, we say they repel.

105
00:04:19,822 --> 00:04:21,052
Repel means push!

106
00:04:21,122 --> 00:04:24,210
Magnets can push each other away, without even touching!

107
00:04:24,230 --> 00:04:27,060
And it depends on which poles are facing each other!

108
00:04:29,765 --> 00:04:30,915
Say it with me!

109
00:04:31,627 --> 00:04:34,607
Magnets can attract (pull) or repel (push) one another.

110
00:04:35,317 --> 00:04:38,127
This depends on which poles are facing each other.

111
00:04:40,602 --> 00:04:42,062
Show me your score hand!

112
00:04:42,342 --> 00:04:43,372
Two fingers?

113
00:04:43,652 --> 00:04:45,022
You beat the Buddies.

114
00:04:45,302 --> 00:04:46,302
High five!

115
00:04:46,880 --> 00:04:48,340
Did you spot the spider?

116
00:04:48,620 --> 00:04:51,330
It was hanging on its silk thread, under the bench!

117
00:04:51,470 --> 00:04:52,780
Here is a fun fact!

118
00:04:52,850 --> 00:04:55,460
Many baby spiders can fly with no wings.

119
00:04:55,520 --> 00:04:58,460
They let out long silk threads, and the wind lifts them up

120
00:04:58,480 --> 00:04:59,530
into the sky!

121
00:04:59,655 --> 00:05:00,935
Tell someone at home!

122
00:05:01,664 --> 00:05:03,864
Let's read today's key words together!

123
00:05:04,154 --> 00:05:04,914
Ready?

124
00:05:05,201 --> 00:05:05,951
Poles.

125
00:05:07,379 --> 00:05:08,359
Attraction.

126
00:05:09,812 --> 00:05:10,642
Repel.

127
00:05:11,999 --> 00:05:12,939
Well done!

128
00:05:13,736 --> 00:05:15,536
A red end and a blue end pull.

129
00:05:15,666 --> 00:05:16,986
Two red ends push.

130
00:05:17,016 --> 00:05:18,636
But what about two blue ends?

131
00:05:18,716 --> 00:05:19,736
Is there a rule?

132
00:05:19,756 --> 00:05:21,346
Find out in Part Two!

133
00:05:22,506 --> 00:05:23,607
Say it with us!

134
00:05:24,407 --> 00:05:25,157
Ready?

135
00:05:25,281 --> 00:05:25,941
One!

136
00:05:26,281 --> 00:05:26,981
two!

137
00:05:27,286 --> 00:05:28,461
Now you know!
